# Model card: ChestX-ray14 metadata classifiers (fairness case study)

## Model details

- **Developer:** Zeineb Jemli, as part of fairaudit {{ results.fairaudit_version }} (MIT license).
- **Models:** scikit-learn logistic regression (baseline and {{ results.experiments | length - 2 }} mitigated variants) and a depth-{{ cfg.tree_max_depth }} decision tree that replicates the original university notebook.
- **Inputs:** follow-up number, patient age and age group, patient sex, view position (PA/AP), original image width/height and pixel spacing. No pixels.
- **Output:** probability that an image has at least one of the 14 ChestX-ray14 findings rather than "No Finding".

## Intended use

- **Intended:** demonstrating and testing fairness auditing and bias mitigation on a real, public medical dataset.
- **Out of scope:** any clinical, diagnostic, triage or screening use. The models never see the image and are only slightly better than chance (ROC AUC around {{ baseline.report.overall.roc_auc | num(2) }}).

