## Caveats and recommendations

- Removing a sensitive attribute ("unawareness") does not remove its proxies; audit the outcome, not the inputs.
- Making one attribute fair can leave others unfair: compare the per-attribute tables in the study report.
- Group-specific thresholds treat groups differently by design, which may be inappropriate or unlawful in some settings.
- In a diagnostic setting, missed findings (low TPR, i.e. under-diagnosis) are usually the costliest error, so the equal opportunity gap deserves the most weight.
- Sex is recorded as binary (M/F) in the source data. Metrics are point estimates on {{ results.splits["test"].n_rows }} test images, without confidence intervals.

